{"output":"I’ll inspect the search code and existing tests, add a minimal stale-request guard, and run the tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nThe controller lets every request update state when it finishes. I’ll add a request counter, incremented even when the query is cleared, and guard results, errors, and loading updates. The existing tests cover normal behavior; I’ll also check the race cases with an inline script without modifying tests.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts with a request counter so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior are unchanged.\n\nVerification:\nnpm test — 4 tests passed.\nnode --input-type=module — inline race and clearing checks passed.\ngit diff --check — passed.\nAll exited 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts with a request counter so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior are unchanged.\n\nVerification:\nnpm test — 4 tests passed.\nnode --input-type=module — inline race and clearing checks passed.\ngit diff --check — passed.\nAll exited 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":10,"tool_calls":[{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-jm2sn40h/1-2-optimized/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":198,"stdout_bytes":0,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-4729065789a0d609ae02841156a8dca1.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test\nsuite_status=$?\nnode --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst items = [{ id: 'new', title: 'New', url: '/new' }];\nfor (const rejectOld of [false, true]) {\n  for (const latestFinishesFirst of [false, true]) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('same');\n    const latest = c.search('same');\n    if (latestFinishesFirst) { requests[1].resolve(items); await latest; }\n    const before = c.getState();\n    if (rejectOld) requests[0].reject(new Error('stale')); else requests[0].resolve([]);\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n    if (!latestFinishesFirst) { requests[1].resolve(items); await latest; }\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'same', results: items, loading: false, error: null });\n  }\n  const requests = [];\n  const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n  const initial = c.search('initial'); requests[0].resolve(items); await initial;\n  const failing = c.search('failure'); requests[1].reject(new Error('error')); await failing;\n  await c.search('');\n  const cleared = { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null };\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), cleared);\n  const pending = c.search('pending');\n  await c.search('  ');\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), cleared);\n  if (rejectOld) requests[2].reject(new Error('stale')); else requests[2].resolve(items);\n  await pending;\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), cleared);\n}\nconsole.log('Race and query-clearing checks passed');\nNODE\nrace_status=$?\ngit diff --check\ncheck_status=$?\ngit diff --stat\ngit diff -- src/search/controller.ts\nprintf '\\nVerification exit codes: suite=%s race=%s diff-check=%s\\n' \"$suite_status\" \"$race_status\" \"$check_status\"\nexit $((suite_status || race_status || check_status))","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-jm2sn40h/1-2-optimized/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":359,"stdout_bytes":2310,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-eb64ff50f40836111ec60663fba50d3d.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":33279,"output_tokens":1212},"usage_details":{"cached_input_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":12}}
